cd /home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon && "$HORIZON_BIN" graph -p Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge add comment label:thm:fga_pic_representability_etale --body "THE WITHDRAWN ZARISKI-SHEAF REASON SURVIVED AT FOUR SITES INCLUDING THE HEADLINE FILE AND THE SHEAF FILE ITSELF -- 'corrected in every .lean and .tex site' was false for nine hours (review-ajc r7, 2026-07-30; fixed in this commit).

WHAT WAS WRONG. Two claims were withdrawn on 2026-07-29 (I-0970, I-0973) and corrected at fgaPicardRepresentability and in the blueprint chapter introduction: (a) that picSharp 'is not a sheaf even Zariski-locally' -- a citation about the ABSOLUTE Pic_X, whereas the RELATIVE functor is Zariski-SEPARATED on these binders (th:cmp part 1; in Lean picSharp_isSheaf_zariski_of_representableBy); and (b) that unconditional picSharp representability is 'FALSE' -- it is conditional in Lean, not_exists_representing_picSharp_of_not_isIso needs an antecedent QUOTED from Kleiman, so the accurate word is 'unproved with a refutation route mapped out'.

BOTH survived, unlabelled, at:
 * Jacobian.lean:41 -- the headline file's own 'why sheafifying works' paragraph, carrying (a) AND (b) in one sentence;
 * Jacobian.lean:783 -- at picardJacobianWitness, the headline definition;
 * PicEtSheaf.lean:150 -- the WORST, because it asserts (a) of relPresheaf BY NAME, i.e. of the relative functor, which is the exact distinction the correction turns on;
 * blueprint Picard_FGAPicRepresentability.tex:1058 and :1106 -- (a) plus 'the predicate is false in general' / 'could not hold'.

WHY THE CORRECTION MISSED THEM, since that is the reusable part: the 2026-07-29 pass grepped the withdrawn CITATION ('not even a Zariski sheaf', 'Kleiman s2 L1292') and fixed every hit. These four sites state the same claim in different words -- 'not a sheaf even Zariski-locally', 'is not a sheaf' -- so they were invisible to a grep seeded from the retracted phrasing. A withdrawn REASON needs a census by proposition, not by phrase.

NOT A NEW MATHEMATICAL FINDING: the seam's own text has been right about this since 2026-07-29. The defect was distributional, and it was concentrated in the two files a reader opens first." 2>&1 | tail -5
